{
  "name": "Maul of Momentum",
  "type": "weapon",
  "img": "modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/icons/items/maul.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Maul), Rare (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p><em>This weighty maul's head is etched with spiraling grooves that seem to pull it forward mid-swing. In motion, it never wants to stop.</em></p><p>You gain a <strong>+1 bonus</strong> to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Unstoppable Drive (1/Day).</strong> On your turn, you can take one additional action, as the Fighter's Action Surge feature. If you already have Action Surge, you instead gain one extra use of it. <strong>Until the end of your next turn, you ignore Difficult Terrain.</strong> This property recharges at dawn.</p><p><strong>Once per turn.</strong> You can gain only one additional action on a given turn, whether it comes from this maul or from Action Surge itself — never both on the same turn.</p><p>When you invoke Unstoppable Drive, the maul's head hums with barely-contained kinetic force, your footfalls crack stone and packed earth, and dust shivers off nearby surfaces — momentum made manifest, and nothing on the battlefield slows you down.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
